From d5f8a69c87df2e75cbf9fa09427a2440bdafa3b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 21:51:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): refusals and backend startup name a leaked
 worker env; scrub TERMINAL_CWD/UI session too [daveey]

Hermes.app pid 59331 (reopened by kanban worker t_45d5a361's `hermes update`) fenced every
Desktop chat with 'delegate_task child contexts cannot mutate Kanban', which never said why.

Detection: top_level_env.leaked_worker_env_diagnosis() reads the lineage card (HERMES_KANBAN_TASK,
else the workspace dir name) from the pinned board and calls the marker leaked when that card is
not running, its worker pid is gone, or this process does not descend from it; it stays silent
when the lineage can't be identified or the board can't be read (a real delegate child or a
worker's own tool subprocess descends from a live running worker). The db fence (kanban_db),
the CLI fast-fail and the tool refusal append it when the fence comes from the env (not an
in-process child), and the serve/dashboard/desktop/gateway startup scrub logs it.

Scrub gap: the shared agent-scope list (9778500b6b) missed the dispatcher's TERMINAL_CWD pin
(file tools/context files anchored in the dead worker's workspace) and the gateway session vars
outside HERMES_SESSION_ (HERMES_UI_SESSION_ID, HERMES_BROWSER_CONTROL_*); a test now pins the list
to gateway.session_context._VAR_MAP. Electron mirror updated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
